From 9f72b7c80d47b51acdca0a8f453932067b8cef90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 22:28:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 5A: investigation rounds + public clues
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New pre-vote flow:
  Private Character Reveal -> Investigation Round 1 -> Investigation
  Round 2 -> Investigation Round 3 (per story) -> existing Voting flow

- New InvestigationRound model (roundNumber, title, publicClue,
  description, discussionPrompt) — public and story-specific, kept
  fully separate from StoryCharacter (identity/secret/alignment stay
  untouched and private, per the existing architecture).
- Story gains investigationRounds[]; all 12 built-in stories ship
  3 unique, story-specific rounds each (spacecraft/museum/court/etc.
  themed, not generic reskins), threaded through the same generator
  used for the character content.
- GameManager gains investigationIndex/currentInvestigationRound()/
  investigationFinished(); this is independent of the existing
  round/clueIndex machinery that drives post-vote clues, so the
  existing voting system is untouched and not duplicated.
- MainActivity: roleReveal's last player now leads into
  investigationStep() instead of straight to startRound(). Each
  round is a single minimal screen (title, public clue, optional
  discussion prompt, one continue button) reusing the existing
  addTitle/addPanel/button/navigation() UI helpers — no UI redesign.
  Once rounds are exhausted (or a story/custom story has none),
  it falls straight through to the existing startRound()/voting flow.
- Custom Story Builder: new step 4/6 lets creators add investigation
  rounds (title + public clue + optional discussion prompt), at
  least one required. Steps renumbered 1-6 accordingly.
- CustomStoryStore reads and writes investigationRounds; older saved
  custom stories without that key load with an empty array and skip
  straight to voting instead of crashing.
- GameManagerTest: added coverage for round count/order/hand-off and
  for the empty-rounds backward-compat path. All 8 tests pass.
- Verified: full javac compile against a faithful Android/org.json
  API stub set (MainActivity + CustomStoryStore), plus a runtime
  smoke test walking investigation->voting for all 12 built-in
  stories.

Not implemented (per scope): Question Cards, special roles, killer
actions/objectives, branching stories, multiple endings, online
sharing/multiplayer, UI redesign.
